<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35412" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνεπι-σκήπτομαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>claim property
				alleged to belong to the state,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνεπισκήψασθαι ἐν τῇ οὐσίᾳ τῇ
					ἐκείνου ἐνοφειλόμενον αὑτῷ ἀργύριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					49.45
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				8.61
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>take proceedings to enforce a claim,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PGurob
				2.28
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
